n"},{"path":"tests/malicious-download-exec/SKILL.md","size":128,"sha256":"041ed32aa0524e563c5aaf5a81d3d9a8b9de982c6e73ed0def22b87de0ed68c0","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"tests/malicious-download-exec/run.sh","size":131,"sha256":"ec0b4c8f173f7eebbf8c0f8425ce5bf73149251ed3c41c917f07b101c887e04e","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"tests/malicious-obfuscated/SKILL.md","size":53,"sha256":"b9da79eddd4eff5ed221d56055f398d4e40fd2ec26e7910d25fb12b99b5139ad","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"tests/malicious-obfuscated/optimize.js","size":296,"sha256":"092d223309982d69ff0f3f7e683e7a9a42ecd9d28c04a3781ed19dc836d14d70","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"tests/malicious-privilege-escalation/SKILL.md","size":95,"sha256":"c5b193dd890bcb25a6b7faa222e2866956d3668a786d6466d646edb1baf1b1cf","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"tests/malicious-privilege-escalation/setup.sh","size":85,"sha256":"5ff6c85406eeac1eac8353c2cf1615f3f00c8f75d162fe843eab9c7e1c2f6d7a","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"tests/malicious-prompt-injection/SKILL.md","size":331,"sha256":"2e4d2a8dffc0432b3a67f8ba4f39bf0459a682652df6d07c16f6d09392021635","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"tests/malicious-symlink/SKILL.md","size":64,"sha256":"12d4db8601635b15921c0471840af0d5a6ef64d546da96c885da76eb0b0f3380","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"tests/malicious-symlink/setup.sh","size":129,"sha256":"cf25ecce441652734479d63ccc282e17195daf5607e54a192683790db8028d3d","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"tests/malicious-sysread/SKILL.md","size":49,"sha256":"9d3d0b971d4648983aea2f96dbafd0726bbf2fda977db5a90c11224158e9a5e0","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"tests/malicious-sysread/monitor.sh","size":221,"sha256":"6028c69822a9d863d2fef5df5c4de77c1f2548d1a121fce00a51d5d9e28fd682","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"tests/malicious-timebomb/SKILL.md","size":56,"sha256":"47aaa40126f80edddb1f8b628692e67f7cddc456cf8973913acea6172af5d8ed","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"tests/malicious-timebomb/scheduler.js","size":322,"sha256":"facd2ffe63d76e35a85f00911fe5278ac9ab3fbb3a4caa8f49454e859a9cef67","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"trust-score.sh","size":8233,"sha256":"3afcebd84484b7b9a32368e3fa5bc72ec0511df017ad5fedce1bab58fb4509b0","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"trust_score.py","size":14110,"sha256":"54682a26c76ba5a1cf031979589199db656376c62c41a049a2c37bc4682acb37","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2187,"sha256":"305813eee2be5e9166eadfa68809dba6681b0066f8f317e0436caae5a9e13d87","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789070434653,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"d5af527a8e72c4c895f67322189d5ac5decb922d33bd655a1f336b3f517c6d59","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/d5af527a8e72c4c895f67322189d5ac5decb922d33bd655a1f336b3f517c6d59","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: yoder-skill-auditor\nVersion: 3.1.0\n\nThis skill bundle is a security scanner designed to detect malicious patterns in other OpenClaw skills. It contains a comprehensive set of checks for credential harvesting, data exfiltration, obfuscation, prompt injection, privilege escalation, and more. The presence of malicious code patterns in the `tests/` directory is intentional, serving as test fixtures to validate the scanner's detection capabilities, and these are explicitly documented as such in `TEST-FIXTURES-WARNING.md` and excluded from the published package via `.clawignore`. The `audit.sh` script includes a `PATTERN_DEF_FILTER` to prevent self-flagging of its own detection logic. There is no evidence that the scanner itself performs any malicious actions, exfiltrates data, or attempts prompt injection against the agent running it. All functionalities are aligned with its stated purpose as a security auditing tool.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779164541179},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":107,"checkedAt":1789070434653},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This appears to be a security-scanner skill, but the inspected artifact includes runnable malicious test scripts and scanner weaknesses that require review before installation.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Local file scanning is proportionate for an auditor, but runnable fixtures that read auth profiles or SSH keys, post to external URLs, download and execute code, or invoke sudo exceed what is needed for distributed scanner tests.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No install hook was found and skill.json lists only top-level scanner files, but the inspected artifact contains tests/ while CHANGELOG.md and TEST-FIXTURES-WARNING.md claim a .clawignore exclusion that is absent.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Normal commands are user-invoked and the test harness scans fixtures rather than executing them, but audit.sh handles attacker-controlled paths unsafely and can be bypassed or abused when scanning untrusted directories.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The normal tools do not create background persistence; trust_score.py writes trend history only when requested, but a shipped privilege-escalation fixture can copy into /usr/local/bin and set a setuid bit if manually run.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The main purpose and required bins, bash and python3, fit a local skill security scanner, but the artifact also contains live credential-exfiltration, remote-code-execution, and privilege-escalation fixtures rather than inert test data.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Do not install this published artifact as-is. Ask the publisher to ship only inert fixture data or exclude tests from the release, restore or verify the test exclusion mechanism, and fix audit.sh path handling and allowlist scoping. If you must evaluate it, do so in a sandbox without credentials, sudo access, or outbound network access.","findings":"[SDI-2] unexpected: Credential-theft examples under tests are relevant to scanner validation, but the inspected files are runnable scripts that read local auth or SSH material and transmit it rather than inert fixtures.\n[SDI-4] unexpected: The obfuscated optimizer sample is located under a malicious test directory, which reduces intent concerns, but if run it decodes an external endpoint, reads an SSH private key, and posts it.\n[SQP-3] unexpected: The time-trigger sample is a detector fixture, but it contains a live date-gated credential-posting path.\n[P1] expected: The CHANGELOG.md phrase is documentation of prompt-injection detection, so that specific documentation occurrence is not itself treated as a malicious instruction.\n[SC2] expected: The CHANGELOG.md curl/wget examples are documentation of detection patterns; the concern comes from the separate runnable download-execute fixture.\n[TP4] expected: Scoring, reporting, benchmarking, and diff auditing are disclosed as auxiliary scanner features; the marketing is overconfident but not independently malicious.\n[T09] unexpected: audit.sh interpolates path variables into python -c snippets and globally downgrades critical findings for basename allowlist matches, creating code-injection and scanner-bypass risks.\n[T03] unexpected: tests/malicious-download-exec/run.sh is present in the inspected tree and contains live remote download-and-execute commands despite documentation claiming tests are excluded from published packages.\n[T04] unexpected: tests/malicious-basic/fetch.sh contains operational credential collection and outbound posting, not merely static text.\n[T05] unexpected: tests/malicious-privilege-escalation/setup.sh invokes sudo and setuid operations; static detector tests should not need live privileged commands.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789070434653}}}}}